# Rank 1075 / CVE-2024-38427: DemoIccMAX's ProfileSequenceId tag parser returned
# false from every path, so a well-formed tag was reported as a parse failure
# (CWE-252 as NVD classifies it). CIccTagXmlProfileSequenceId::ParseXml walked
# the ProfileIdDesc children, built each entry, and then fell off the end into
#
#   return false;
#
# with no `return true` anywhere in the function. Pool commit f891074a0f is the
# fix: the merge of pull request #66, whose IccTagXml.cpp hunk is the one
# character the advisory names, and whose other half fixes an unrelated compile
# error in IccUtil.cpp. The advisory cites the individual commit 85ce74e inside
# that pull request, which is why the metadata check reported COMMIT_MISMATCH
# against the merge; the row names the merge that carries it, so it stands.
# No pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, and the honest reason is that the shape is checkable while the
# security reading of it is not. "A function declared to return bool with no
# path returning true" is a property any pass over the return statements can
# state, and it is what separates these two revisions exactly. What it is not is
# a weakness: a predicate stuck at false fails closed, and code that fails closed
# is the safe direction. The dangerous form is the mirror image, a validator or
# verifier stuck at true, and that is what the ontology already reaches for --
# code.EmptyVerifierAcceptance with VYQL-AUTH-006 is a verifier that accepts when
# it should not. Minting for the always-false direction would report every
# fail-closed helper in every codebase, which is the precision cost this campaign
# has already declined three times.
#
# So this rank is not evidence that a rule is missing. It is a functional
# regression that received a security identifier, and the useful record is that
# the class it would belong to points the other way. Scanning the file reports
# 170 findings, four at or above high, none of them on this function.
#
# The two snippets differ only in the value the last statement returns.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-precision-cost

test "rank1075: the tag parser cannot report success"
  lang cpp
  file IccXML/IccLibXML/IccTagXml.cpp
  reject VYQL-AUTH-006
  code
  ```
  #include <string>

  bool CIccTagXmlProfileSequenceId::ParseXml(xmlNode *pNode, std::string &parseStr)
  {
      if (!pNode)
          return false;

      for (pNode = icXmlFindNode(pNode->children, "ProfileIdDesc"); pNode;
           pNode = icXmlFindNode(pNode->next, "ProfileIdDesc")) {
          CIccProfileIdDesc entry;

          const char *szDesc = icXmlAttrValue(pNode, "profileID");
          if (szDesc && *szDesc)
              entry.m_profileID = szDesc;

          m_list->push_back(entry);
      }

      return false;
  }
  ```

test "rank1075: the same parser returning success"
  lang cpp
  file IccXML/IccLibXML/IccTagXml.cpp
  reject VYQL-AUTH-006
  code
  ```
  #include <string>

  bool CIccTagXmlProfileSequenceId::ParseXml(xmlNode *pNode, std::string &parseStr)
  {
      if (!pNode)
          return false;

      for (pNode = icXmlFindNode(pNode->children, "ProfileIdDesc"); pNode;
           pNode = icXmlFindNode(pNode->next, "ProfileIdDesc")) {
          CIccProfileIdDesc entry;

          const char *szDesc = icXmlAttrValue(pNode, "profileID");
          if (szDesc && *szDesc)
              entry.m_profileID = szDesc;

          m_list->push_back(entry);
      }

      return true;
  }
